andromeda: before the framebuffer's CPU copy of a surface, let the GPU finish the
Metal work already submitted and clean the surface from the CPU caches
(andromeda_fbsync_before_read in bsd/dev/andromeda_gpu_mtl.c, declared in
andromeda_gpu_present.h; off unless andrmtl is on, andrfbsync=0 disables).
With Metal, backboardd swaps right after its submit and the copy read
half-drawn or stale frames.

diff --git a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp
--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp
@@ -508,6 +508,9 @@
 			continue;
 		}
 		uintptr_t src = s->kernelAddress();
+		if (src != 0) {
+			andromeda_fbsync_before_read(src, (uint64_t)s->bytesPerRow * s->height);
+		}
 		uint32_t bpe = s->bytesPerElement ? s->bytesPerElement : 4;
 		if (w <= 0 || h <= 0) {
 			w = (int32_t)s->width;
